__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.venv/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
~$*
*.tmp

# canon slotting staging (AGENTS.md §3 _wip; not authority)
# CD-128: `_inbox/` -> `_inbox/*` + an un-ignored README, the CD-126 / `_unvendored/` form.
# The staged files stay out of Git; the NOTE that says why they are staged goes in. A retention
# reason written into a gitignored file is per-machine, so the next sweep on another device would
# re-raise the same four PDFs a fourth time — which is the thing §12.7's three-session rule was
# supposed to end.
_inbox/*
!_inbox/README.md

# Render artifact retention (CD-024): evidence stays, scratch goes.
# Anything a SMOKE.md cites as proof lives under an evidence/ folder and IS committed.
# Page rasters produced while verifying are regenerable and are not evidence.
# Widened CD-046: `**/_wip/*.png` matched only PNGs sitting directly in a _wip/, so a
# scratch raster one folder deeper (canon/_wip/c5-eng-raster/) would have been committed
# as if it were evidence — the exact outcome CD-024 exists to prevent.
**/_wip/**/*.png
!**/evidence/*.png

# Parked-not-vendored (session 3): the note is committed, the binaries are not.
# See _unvendored/README.md — a file with no consumer is not an Assets-class file (AGENTS.md 12.1).
_unvendored/*
!_unvendored/README.md
